# Safe Firewall Configuration for Cursor Compatibility

## Understanding the Requirements

1. **Cursor needs OUTGOING connections** to connect to its servers
   - Domains: `*.cursor.sh`, `*.cursor-cdn.com`, `*.cursorapi.com`
   - Protocols: HTTPS (TLS 1.2+), HTTP/2, HTTP/1.1
   - Ports: 443 (HTTPS), 80 (HTTP fallback)
2. **GitHub needs OUTGOING connections** for Git operations
   - Domains: `github.com`, `api.github.com`, `*.github.com`, `*.githubusercontent.com`
   - Protocols: HTTPS (443), SSH (22), Git protocol (9418)
   - Required for: git clone, push, pull, GitHub Actions, Packages
3. **Windsurf needs OUTGOING connections** to connect to its servers
   - Domains: `*.windsurf.com`, `*.codeium.com`, `*.codeiumdata.com`
   - Protocols: HTTPS (TLS 1.2+)
   - Ports: 443 (HTTPS)
   - Required for: AI coding assistant, agent execution, model responses
4. **We need INCOMING SSH** only from Tailscale
4. **We need INCOMING HTTP/HTTPS** for public website access
5. **We need ESTABLISHED connections** for responses to outgoing requests

## Logical Firewall Rules

```bash
# 1. Allow all OUTGOING (for Cursor, npm, apt, etc.)
sudo ufw default allow outgoing

# 2. Deny all INCOMING by default (blocks attacks)
sudo ufw default deny incoming

# 3. Allow ESTABLISHED/RELATED connections (responses to our outgoing requests)
sudo ufw allow in on lo
sudo ufw allow in proto tcp from any to any port 22 state ESTABLISHED,RELATED

# 4. Allow SSH ONLY from Tailscale network
sudo ufw allow from 100.64.0.0/10 to any port 22 comment 'SSH via Tailscale'

# 5. Allow HTTP/HTTPS for public website
sudo ufw allow 80/tcp comment 'HTTP'
sudo ufw allow 443/tcp comment 'HTTPS'

# 6. Allow established connections for HTTP/HTTPS responses
sudo ufw allow in proto tcp from any to any port 80,443 state ESTABLISHED,RELATED
```

## Why This Works

- ✅ **Outgoing allowed:** Cursor can connect to its servers
  - All Cursor domains accessible: `*.cursor.sh`, `*.cursor-cdn.com`, `*.cursorapi.com`
  - HTTP/2 and HTTP/1.1 streaming supported
  - TLS 1.2+ connections work
- ✅ **Outgoing allowed:** GitHub access works
  - All GitHub domains accessible: `github.com`, `api.github.com`, `*.github.com`, `*.githubusercontent.com`
  - HTTPS (443) for web and API
  - SSH (22) for git operations
  - Git protocol (9418) if needed
- ✅ **Outgoing allowed:** Windsurf access works
  - All Windsurf domains accessible: `*.windsurf.com`, `*.codeium.com`, `*.codeiumdata.com`
  - HTTPS (443) for all services
  - TLS 1.2+ connections work
- ✅ **Incoming SSH restricted:** Only from Tailscale network
- ✅ **Incoming HTTP/HTTPS allowed:** Public website access
- ✅ **Established connections:** Responses to outgoing requests work
- ✅ **No lockout risk:** Tailscale SSH access maintained

## Cursor Network Requirements

Based on [Cursor's network configuration docs](https://cursor.com/docs/enterprise/network-configuration):

**Required Domains:**
- `*.cursor.sh` (main API and services)
- `*.cursor-cdn.com` (CDN resources)
- `*.cursorapi.com` (API endpoints)

**Required Protocols:**
- HTTPS (port 443) - TLS 1.2 or higher
- HTTP/2 bidirectional streaming
- HTTP/1.1 Server-Side Events (SSE) fallback

**Note:** Cursor doesn't provide static IP lists (they change). Use domain-based allowlisting or allow all HTTPS outgoing (current configuration).

## GitHub Network Requirements

GitHub requires access to multiple domains and ports for full functionality:

**Required Domains:**
- `github.com` (main website and Git operations)
- `api.github.com` (REST API)
- `*.github.com` (various GitHub services)
- `*.githubusercontent.com` (raw content, releases, assets)
- `github-releases.githubusercontent.com` (release downloads)
- `codeload.github.com` (code downloads)

**Required Ports:**
- **HTTPS (443):** Primary method for Git operations (`git clone https://...`)
- **SSH (22):** For Git over SSH (`git clone git@github.com:...`)
- **Git Protocol (9418):** Legacy protocol (rarely used)

**Common Operations:**
- `git clone`, `git push`, `git pull` (HTTPS or SSH)
- GitHub Actions (if using self-hosted runners)
- GitHub Packages (npm, Docker, etc.)
- GitHub API calls
- Release downloads

**Note:** GitHub uses dynamic IP addresses. Allow all outgoing HTTPS/SSH or use domain-based allowlisting. Our configuration (allow all outgoing) supports all GitHub operations.

## Windsurf Network Requirements

Windsurf (AI coding assistant) requires access to specific domains for full functionality:

**Required Domains:**
- `*.windsurf.com` (main Windsurf services)
- `*.codeium.com` (Codeium backend services)
- `*.codeiumdata.com` (Codeium data services)

**Required Ports:**
- **HTTPS (443):** Primary protocol for all Windsurf operations

**Common Operations:**
- AI coding assistant features
- Agent execution
- Model responses and prompts
- Editor loading and functionality
- JetBrains IDE plugin (if used)

**Important Notes:**
- Blocking these domains may prevent:
  - Editor from loading
  - Agent execution
  - Models being unresponsive to prompts
- Windsurf uses dynamic IP addresses (they change over time)
- **Recommendation:** Use domain-based allowlisting rather than IP addresses
- Our configuration (allow all outgoing HTTPS) supports all Windsurf operations

**Sources:**
- [Windsurf Troubleshooting](https://docs.windsurf.com/troubleshooting/windsurf-common-issues)
- [Windsurf Security](https://windsurf.com/security)

## Safe Implementation Steps

1. **Open a backup SSH session via Tailscale** (in case primary drops)
2. **Configure rules** (firewall still inactive)
3. **Verify rules** are correct
4. **Enable firewall** only if rules look good
5. **Test Cursor connection** immediately after enabling

## Complete Safe Command

```bash
# Step 1: Configure rules (firewall still inactive)
sudo ufw default allow outgoing  # Allows Cursor, npm, apt, etc.
sudo ufw default deny incoming

# Allow established/related connections (for responses)
sudo ufw allow in on lo
sudo ufw allow in proto tcp from any to any port 22 state ESTABLISHED,RELATED
sudo ufw allow in proto tcp from any to any port 80,443 state ESTABLISHED,RELATED

# Allow SSH from Tailscale
sudo ufw allow from 100.64.0.0/10 to any port 22 comment 'SSH via Tailscale'

# Allow public HTTP/HTTPS
sudo ufw allow 80/tcp comment 'HTTP'
sudo ufw allow 443/tcp comment 'HTTPS'

# Step 2: Verify rules
sudo ufw status verbose

# Step 3: Enable only if rules are correct
sudo ufw --force enable

# Step 4: Test immediately
curl -I https://aicomply.dev

# Step 5: Test Cursor connectivity
curl -v https://api2.cursor.sh |& grep -C1 issuer:
# Should see "Amazon RSA" (not your proxy/provider)

# Step 6: Test Windsurf connectivity
curl -I https://windsurf.com
curl -I https://codeium.com
```

## Testing Cursor Connectivity

After enabling firewall, test Cursor's connectivity:

**Test basic connectivity:**
```bash
curl -v https://api2.cursor.sh |& grep -C1 issuer:
```
Should show "Amazon RSA" certificate. If you see your proxy/provider, SSL inspection is active.

**Test HTTP/1.1 streaming (SSE fallback):**
```bash
echo -ne "\x0\x0\x0\x0\x11{\"payload\":\"foo\"}" | \
  curl --http1.1 -No - -XPOST \
  -H "Content-Type: application/connect+json" \
  --data-binary @- \
  https://api2.cursor.sh/aiserver.v1.HealthService/StreamSSE
```
Output should appear line by line over 5 seconds.

**Test HTTP/2 bidirectional streaming:**
```bash
(for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do \
  echo -ne "\x0\x0\x0\x0\x12{\"payload\":\"foo$i\"}"; \
  sleep 1; \
done) | curl -No - -XPOST \
  -H "Content-Type: application/connect+json" \
  -T - \
  https://api2.cursor.sh/aiserver.v1.HealthService/StreamBidi
```
Output should appear once per second.

## What Gets Allowed/Blocked

### ✅ ALLOWED (Incoming)
- SSH from Tailscale network (100.64.0.0/10)
- HTTP (port 80) - public website
- HTTPS (port 443) - public website
- Established/Related connections (responses)

### ✅ ALLOWED (Outgoing)
- **Everything** - Cursor, Windsurf, GitHub, npm, apt, curl, etc.
- **Cursor domains:** `*.cursor.sh`, `*.cursor-cdn.com`, `*.cursorapi.com`
- **Windsurf domains:** `*.windsurf.com`, `*.codeium.com`, `*.codeiumdata.com`
- **GitHub domains:** `github.com`, `api.github.com`, `*.github.com`, `*.githubusercontent.com`
- **HTTPS (443):** All domains (for Cursor, Windsurf, GitHub, npm, etc.)
- **SSH (22):** All domains (for Git over SSH)
- **HTTP (80):** All domains (fallback)
- **DNS (53):** For domain resolution
- **Git Protocol (9418):** If needed for legacy Git operations

### ❌ BLOCKED (Incoming)
- Direct SSH from internet (only Tailscale allowed)
- All other ports
- Unauthorized connections

## Testing After Enable

1. **Test website:** `curl -I https://aicomply.dev`
2. **Test Cursor:** Try to connect/use Cursor
3. **Test Windsurf:** Try to connect/use Windsurf
4. **Test GitHub HTTPS:** `curl -I https://github.com`
5. **Test GitHub API:** `curl -I https://api.github.com`
6. **Test Git over HTTPS:** `git ls-remote https://github.com/octocat/Hello-World.git`
7. **Test Git over SSH:** `ssh -T git@github.com` (if SSH keys configured)
8. **Test Windsurf domains:**
   - `curl -I https://windsurf.com`
   - `curl -I https://codeium.com`
9. **Test SSH via Tailscale:** Connect from your machine
10. **Test SSH from internet:** Should be blocked

---

**Key Point:** Outgoing is always allowed, so Cursor will work!
